\section{Setting a limit}{

Each option takes a single number, 0 or more; \code{Inf} removes the limit.
Any other value is an error when the option is read. The error of class
\code{spatialkit_work_limit} carries \code{work} (the count), \code{limit} and \code{what}
(the step), and its message says what to change: for a fit, fewer
starts, a coarser \code{obs_per_cell}, random starts of the density kind or a
higher limit; for a search, reinstalling \pkg{FNN}. A
profile just below \code{spatialkit.fit_work_max} prints nothing while its
fits run.

The console log is set with \code{\link[=spatialkit_quiet]{spatialkit_quiet()}}, not with an option.
}

